f1-42011f4d99a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-120546" :question/problem "Let $A(1,0,-1)$ and $B(0,1,1).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively." :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i-k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(i-k)+2(j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120546/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120546"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120543/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "aea2f69d-9ad5-5eaf-9d63-ca8e6650f777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120543/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "01cf21bf-1d9b-52bc-9ed8-a0b81f0b1c51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120543/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4a5dc535-521e-515c-9334-539e36ae461e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120543/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" :answer/id #uuid "751c70b9-f198-5081-b5d2-f4b011a45533" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120543/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "51c0a073-