egin{aligned}a-b & =(5i+9k)-(3i+9j+8k) \\\\  & =2i-9j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a-b| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{86}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101003/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection/aad2f73b3d98c2c84885833ca81999af73544acae72b64f9df8052ce456f5e03" :answer/id #uuid "b992565f-df29-5c4a-a4b0-dd51fa1b2908" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{101}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection/b97391586db4edd696a0261f6f0570a22bae2ecb444cd68f1b312a9c002f2b1d" :answer/id #uuid "1af54d5b-75af-57f3-9136-aefd064108b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection/00e03e50392eab22ac426bf0eede81fb51c2fe3fb78a07fc58e021b008d91ba8" :answer/id #uuid "85a9d8f8-65da-5299-8573-c07fac97a7be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{103}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection/b4a50f1a326162632b421be24d1154f5762fe56422d646518587f3f5396378d0" :answer/id #uuid "89553c56-3ebe-53f6-8083-a53c4e80d44a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{102}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "ad0918e2-668d-5b3d-a358-cbc9bad7897e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "960015a6-e2d4-5760-b835-46450522c98c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70425/selection/aad2f73b3d98c2c84885833ca81999af73544acae72b64f9df8052ce456f5e03" :answer-field/choices ["q-70425/selection/aad2f73b3d98c2c84885833ca81999af73544acae72b64f9df8052ce456f5e03" "q-70425/selection/b97391586db4edd696a0261f6f0570a22bae2ecb444cd68f1b312a9c002f2b1d" "q-70425/selection/00e03e50392eab22ac426bf0eede81fb51c2fe3fb78a07fc58e021b008d91ba8" "q-70425/selection/b4a50f1a326162632b421be24d1154f5762fe56422d646518587f3f5396378d0" "q-70425/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70425" :question/id #uuid "987674d8-6a5b-5010-97df-7f67935f50cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-70425" :question/problem "Let $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,-3).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively." :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=i+3j-3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(2i+j)+2(i+3j-3k) \\\\  & =4i+7j-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+49+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{101}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70425/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281595/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer/id #uuid "36dccfda-4853-5561-980a-992914ea0c54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281595/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ad6d6a-7f9e-5e2a-8741-100ce4cb292b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281595/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer-field/choices ["q-281595/field-1/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281595" :question/id #uuid "09cc540a-0811-50ab-be39-1fa66c3fe0c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281595" :question/problem "Let $P(1,-2,4)$ and $Q(-3,0,5).$ Find $|q-p|,$ where $p$ and $q$ are position vectors of $P$ and $Q$, respectively.\n\n$|q-p|=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =p=i-2j+4k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =q=-3i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $q-p,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-p & =(-3i+5k)-(i-2j+4k) \\\\  & =-4i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|q-p| & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281595/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-18975"] :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $a$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{77}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{77}}\\cdot ⟨-2,8,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}},\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}},\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection/87a453a31414b6ce9384e05b82e3bafd903ea206aeffee13e0c7e5e8242e569a" :answer/id #uuid "61f2c3dd-7124-5c52-ab67-2350d99e05aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection/5e203e4f551a20d889e408f7e3c016b4ac08719a8cb395286188a7ffb31ec6e9" :answer/id #uuid "c0f6c572-bb2e-50ae-b973-dc693af85c1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection/37170d02c8550af122b9f9ff1d696d03c004fafb9a2b43096b54396d41a19daa" :answer/id #uuid "595818e4-7608-5319-8879-68af7ebd600c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection/cdd67693d6079c766b1a93d662fa05fdaa28c605fe90f4c0838bf6ce4e0f9c57" :answer/id #uuid "8f6987be-beef-53a1-9827-da8122beba19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection/545d473cb0bbbc06a0e28a1e8cfe08bedd11e9b717f295cb914fea8d3077d4f0" :answer/id #uuid "0cf7fd18-68f7-5d5b-a739-d880bf2f1e02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b2af0e-0b1d-533b-bcda-fea92242b130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101015/selection/87a453a31414b6ce9384e05b82e3bafd903ea206aeffee13e0c7e5e8242e569a" :answer-field/choices ["q-101015/selection/87a453a31414b6ce9384e05b82e3bafd903ea206aeffee13e0c7e5e8242e569a" "q-101015/selection/5e203e4f551a20d889e408f7e3c016b4ac08719a8cb395286188a7ffb31ec6e9" "q-101015/selection/37170d02c8550af122b9f9ff1d696d03c004fafb9a2b43096b54396d41a19daa" "q-101015/selection/cdd67693d6079c766b1a93d662fa05fdaa28c605fe90f4c0838bf6ce4e0f9c57" "q-101015/selection/545d473cb0bbbc06a0e28a1e8cfe08bedd11e9b717f295cb914fea8d3077d4f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101015" :question/id #uuid "37c26371-ee5e-53be-9050-103fa05959ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-101015" :question/problem "Given that $c=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,c\\,| & =\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $c$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}c \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-101015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "bef966c5-dfeb-5d2e-88f6-054d460a46b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "348944cd-485a-5a2d-89d3-38c42c33c79d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae50204b-f4a7-50a1-950e-93908aafa15c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281600/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer-field/choices ["q-281600/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-281600/field-1/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600/field-2/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "7b07c50d-63c8-54a0-8e9e-84b9f064ed61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee458d5-4e9f-5487-a55d-1a9c17a9eda7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281600/field-2/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-281600/field-2/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281600" :question/id #uuid "9e5eb066-bcdc-5c6c-bd00-a9b20ee93a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-281600" :question/problem "Given that $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $n.$\n\n|  |  | $-\\frac{2}{3}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $u=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,n\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}n \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281600/field-1" "q-281600/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281600"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection/d941b457eb1c6ef404eeaac4deef961b67e6ccc70427bd73103547e90c891fd4" :answer/id #uuid "bdacf46e-c1a3-5672-a5a1-23da5e669d11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{3}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection/369cc73cec445f09546ff5ae40f1fa68c8f34d3312bc2681a40eb0fe56159e09" :answer/id #uuid "a71b06b0-fb26-5ce9-af8c-f3efed43861f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{26}},0,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{26}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection/9743f7cb783d7abbfaef6fbafb492a9caa42e31a82efd60364437d3678b5fabd" :answer/id #uuid "a0a2405a-2453-500b-93b8-2857c42c4c65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{5},0,\\frac{3}{5}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection/9126179b582fda63d84339162039fd372c8420288d07710e1f4508b155aa6fa0" :answer/id #uuid "aa3a865d-72dd-55fd-9ade-4c029df7b76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{23}},0,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{23}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection/dfe94da064cde8d33f450abbd3bdb95859c1bd4b6b31a7f3f9cb90f1ef584be1" :answer/id #uuid "892330d6-9f66-5b8f-bb9f-6e9413045c75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},0,\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{6}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b71d6cb0-c834-5f2f-8302-599f0e0053ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70430/selection/9743f7cb783d7abbfaef6fbafb492a9caa42e31a82efd60364437d3678b5fabd" :answer-field/choices ["q-70430/selection/d941b457eb1c6ef404eeaac4deef961b67e6ccc70427bd73103547e90c891fd4" "q-70430/selection/369cc73cec445f09546ff5ae40f1fa68c8f34d3312bc2681a40eb0fe56159e09" "q-70430/selection/9743f7cb783d7abbfaef6fbafb492a9caa42e31a82efd60364437d3678b5fabd" "q-70430/selection/9126179b582fda63d84339162039fd372c8420288d07710e1f4508b155aa6fa0" "q-70430/selection/dfe94da064cde8d33f450abbd3bdb95859c1bd4b6b31a7f3f9cb90f1ef584be1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70430" :question/id #uuid "9d11fcaf-d601-5df3-a05e-e3ba6cc96f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-70430" :question/problem "Let $v=⟨-4,0,3⟩.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $v.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{|\\,v\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,v\\,| & =\\sqrt{{v}_{x}^{2}+{v}_{y}^{2}+{v}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $v$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{|\\,v\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ⟨-4,0,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5},0,\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70430/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70430"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" :answer/id #uuid "b9d8ecd1-ff3d-5b20-a571-e158d988a6af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection/992684758c8365f1c05cfb85a1c08aa7e08bb02abc0f9817c54b1b318810ca84" :answer/id #uuid "499517ce-8370-587b-993c-91301caffa25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection/5f36469e454cb236b32040d924c8b047edc539a66baa8fb01ca9c5a4584caf79" :answer/id #uuid "e85c0d1d-f843-5670-9623-127449b9d4c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection/18adc8eb67c0b0792a4c3b3bcda3733259a31cf251a90a650183ca75144f605b" :answer/id #uuid "a0f0855f-67d1-5bbe-bc62-f378c8eddb59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection/229194fc7dc19514d20d9ad5dc0e2ddb7186ea63e9ad021b9d6c3fce938f23f4" :answer/id #uuid "6cdbe149-04ab-5ff6-9a42-6aab4426470a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "25e2a601-14e5-57e7-a166-5ec14a51289f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18977/selection/5f36469e454cb236b32040d924c8b047edc539a66baa8fb01ca9c5a4584caf79" :answer-field/choices ["q-18977/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" "q-18977/selection/992684758c8365f1c05cfb85a1c08aa7e08bb02abc0f9817c54b1b318810ca84" "q-18977/selection/5f36469e454cb236b32040d924c8b047edc539a66baa8fb01ca9c5a4584caf79" "q-18977/selection/18adc8eb67c0b0792a4c3b3bcda3733259a31cf251a90a650183ca75144f605b" "q-18977/selection/229194fc7dc19514d20d9ad5dc0e2ddb7186ea63e9ad021b9d6c3fce938f23f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18977" :question/id #uuid "4aedad12-e4e4-5e62-ae83-35382ca40566" :question/math-academy-id "q-18977" :question/problem "Given that $c=⟨-1,0,1⟩$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,c\\,| & =\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $c$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{c}{|c|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot ⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "8bd7219f-6907-5f1d-afba-8dbe888f807f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" :answer/id #uuid "a6c9577e-1896-59d8-b930-6e9b9f755bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "1d4f8682-7e56-5c76-8be9-35af48c7e09b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" :answer/id #uuid "f0ed6c28-59e3-505b-83ae-05e37746cf5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "327084be-a9cb-511b-bd8a-4a0bebcbb1ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecba19e6-9a28-5e85-a00a-81683edd3f96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18309/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" :answer-field/choices ["q-18309/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" "q-18309/selection/7336f16cf9437bd809ce5e09d7dc666eb175d0cf5c31ff077c77f0542ed57f13" "q-18309/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-18309/selection/5cfe33d704dbba0d7c6cb0e4c8b69c5862cecddd6652e8decd2b6e71b500b63d" "q-18309/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18309" :question/id #uuid "d760a7fb-7cfa-5c14-a94a-ab89ef422900" :question/math-academy-id "q-18309" :question/problem "Let $A(5,-1,1)$ and $B(0,-2,3).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=5i-j+k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=-2j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j+3k)-(5i-j+k) \\\\  & =-5i-j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-18309/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18309"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection/a83c57d39a250871ea5b155fa09c0f7a09b6fb139843790c64e48e9fb55fd081" :answer/id #uuid "fdebd7c2-31aa-553e-83c8-b92199c5d24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection/97b8876803ef4c670b94fa583326616be00d9a183c62c8e91ab6d0e6e264a463" :answer/id #uuid "f63024e9-c5d2-5550-aa05-d23ba72ca4db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection/1c1cfa6294746e0c3b1d39e58af916209fa55cb93883bb5c06163d71bd828d1d" :answer/id #uuid "1eff147d-7991-5577-941f-dfefef771a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection/a74d9c74860de29fb8d1d14e91ed165d8f275036309c2fdf90e7bb5600b640a4" :answer/id #uuid "3c8a0d37-81c7-5dff-b38d-e85609370fe6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection/4c1c8b2a924372ebbcdbb011574db2ad95437a3447ef79afd0942e8921dcfd72" :answer/id #uuid "e24ab795-753f-51df-a4e5-23471241d90f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4f24e8-2b08-509d-8782-662496fe1685" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101022/selection/97b8876803ef4c670b94fa583326616be00d9a183c62c8e91ab6d0e6e264a463" :answer-field/choices ["q-101022/selection/a83c57d39a250871ea5b155fa09c0f7a09b6fb139843790c64e48e9fb55fd081" "q-101022/selection/97b8876803ef4c670b94fa583326616be00d9a183c62c8e91ab6d0e6e264a463" "q-101022/selection/1c1cfa6294746e0c3b1d39e58af916209fa55cb93883bb5c06163d71bd828d1d" "q-101022/selection/a74d9c74860de29fb8d1d14e91ed165d8f275036309c2fdf90e7bb5600b640a4" "q-101022/selection/4c1c8b2a924372ebbcdbb011574db2ad95437a3447ef79afd0942e8921dcfd72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101022" :question/id #uuid "ed7c86d6-fb53-53c2-abe3-3eb800a8608d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101022" :question/problem "Let $A(2,7,0)$ and $B(2,5,4).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{AB}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+7j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=2i+5j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =2i+5j+4k-(2i+7j) \\\\  & =-2j+4k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot ⟨0,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-101022/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101022"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281689/field-1/8f99b8acb2edc71c05684b50cbc9dfddf7e570068b74b2f97df96b071330abfe" :answer/id #uuid "bd417ad9-e6a2-589c-be4f-93c2f63606fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{89}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281689/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6bfb3b44-e1e4-5492-8fd9-e32e311a31f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281689/field-1/8f99b8acb2edc71c05684b50cbc9dfddf7e570068b74b2f97df96b071330abfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-281689/field-1/8f99b8acb2edc71c05684b50cbc9dfddf7e570068b74b2f97df96b071330abfe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281689" :question/id #uuid "da6cd2a0-d46a-5b1d-903b-d302fcd58f5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-281689" :question/problem "Let $C(2,4,-3)$ and $D(-1,0,5).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{DC}|.$\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{DC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OC} & =c=2i+4j-3k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OD} & =d=-i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{DC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OD} \\\\  & =c-d \\\\  & =(2i+4j-3k)-(-i+5k) \\\\  & =3i+4j-8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{DC}| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{89}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281689/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351/field-1/32cae6ab0a27a3f93edc21be63f72f8215fc1cb3cdab513f35ebe4bc54c7efc3" :answer/id #uuid "7a2a4f49-1c19-57fb-9a47-02edfebab8e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c2579090-718e-57e8-8ad7-21842b355a64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "32e1507d-3844-5fe6-b8ec-acb94d8025a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282351/field-1/32cae6ab0a27a3f93edc21be63f72f8215fc1cb3cdab513f35ebe4bc54c7efc3" :answer-field/choices ["q-282351/field-1/32cae6ab0a27a3f93edc21be63f72f8215fc1cb3cdab513f35ebe4bc54c7efc3" "q-282351/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351/field-2/f231606239ad8e7def0e910c6a81af10773e30fa177a2db0c17ce78daaa0d35a" :answer/id #uuid "7dd2998c-06ce-5201-bc18-2c28c9c17ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea830354-4a32-5044-aee0-4689e6cb87d6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282351/field-2/f231606239ad8e7def0e910c6a81af10773e30fa177a2db0c17ce78daaa0d35a" :answer-field/choices ["q-282351/field-2/f231606239ad8e7def0e910c6a81af10773e30fa177a2db0c17ce78daaa0d35a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282351" :question/id #uuid "f574a23c-91ca-57cf-8977-20c4b56285cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-282351" :question/problem "Let $A(3,-2,-1)$ and $B(3,-2,0).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $-2a+b.$\n\n$u=⟨${{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=3i-2j-k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=3i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $-2a+b$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =-2(3i-2j-k)+(3i-2j) \\\\  & =-6i+4j+2k+3i-2j \\\\  & =-3i+2j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{-2a+b}{|\\,-2a+b\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we divide the vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\cdot ⟨-3,2,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}},\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}},\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-282351/field-1" "q-282351/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282351"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-282324/field-1/a4c9841c0c3d220d0d41a17f1b4a78aa474e43b184e2f7cf44b8bbdcd320b434" :answer/id #uuid "bca73923-98e8-597f-b98e-0c51dd30f950" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282324/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d7b1a13-2fae-58e2-ba0f-db57c176bc23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282324/field-1/a4c9841c0c3d220d0d41a17f1b4a78aa474e43b184e2f7cf44b8bbdcd320b434" :answer-field/choices ["q-282324/field-1/a4c9841c0c3d220d0d41a17f1b4a78aa474e43b184e2f7cf44b8bbdcd320b434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282324/field-2/6a59bb52cc7c09aa6e1cece2fb1c4ae1215f68e245f0baf5dd3989901fe19e3f" :answer/id #uuid "20040203-50f8-5150-80b2-55422c07024c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-282324/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "28e35acb-1c15-5bc8-a28d-8ac27319acad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-282324/field-2/6a59bb52cc7c09aa6e1cece2fb1c4ae1215f68e245f0baf5dd3989901fe19e3f" :answer-field/choices ["q-282324/field-2/6a59bb52cc7c09aa6e1cece2fb1c4ae1215f68e245f0baf5dd3989901fe19e3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-282324" :question/id #uuid "29d6a356-c63e-5c97-b3cf-34173a5ab8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-282324" :question/problem "Let $R(5,-3,2)$ and $S(1,-1,4).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{SR}.$\n\n$u=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =r=5i-3j+2k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OS} & =s=i-j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{SR}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =r-s \\\\  & =(5i-3j+2k)-(i-j+4k) \\\\  & =4i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{SR}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{SR}\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{SR}| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\overset{\\to }{SR}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{SR}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{SR}\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\overset{\\to }{SR} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot ⟨4,-2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-282324/field-1" "q-282324/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-282324"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
